StarAI Viola robot description (Seeed Studio / FashionStar)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:  https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/fashionstar-starai-arm-ros2
Commit:  be498c0034f30bfbe1ceacafeb773ffd95309a69
Path:    src/viola_description/

Upstream ships no license file, and its package.xml declares
"TODO: License declaration". The files are included here so the simulation
runs without a ROS 2 workspace. If you are the rights holder and want them
removed or labelled differently, open an issue.

  assets/viola/meshes/*.STL
      The nine meshes, byte-identical to upstream.

  assets/viola/urdf/viola.urdf
      upstream urdf/viola_description.urdf with four changes:
        1. Mesh paths: package://viola_description/meshes/... became
           ../meshes/... so the file loads without a ROS package path.
        2. joint1 axis: 7.6e-05 0 -0.999999997 became 0 0 -1.
        3. joint7_right limits: -3.14..3.14 became -0.03..0, the same range
           upstream gives joint7_left, which it mimics.
        4. Line endings: CRLF became LF.
      The header comment is upstream's and is unchanged.

Derived from those files by the scripts in this repository:

  assets/viola/urdf/viola.xrdf     scripts/make_viola_xrdf.py
  assets/viola/usd/viola/          scripts/import_viola.py

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Required at run time, not included
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NVIDIA Isaac Sim 6.0.1, including its Pink inverse-kinematics extension
(isaacsim.robot_motion.pink) and its cuMotion extension
(isaacsim.robot_motion.cumotion). Isaac Sim is installed separately and is
covered by NVIDIA's own license terms.
